   "noun": "kaze",
   "particle": "ga",
   "verb": "naoru",
   "verbJa": "治る",
   "verbSense": "heal, get better (an illness, an injury); the same-sounding naoru also means a thing gets fixed",
   "englishVerb": "get over",
   "trap": null,
   "partners": [
    "kega (injury)",
    "byouki (illness)",
    "kizu (wound)"
   ],
   "flags": [],
   "use": "Asked after someone's cold as kaze naotta? and answered mou naotta or mada naoranai. Ga drops, and kaze itself is often left out once the topic is clear.",
   "notes": "Hayaku naoshite ne (get well soon) uses the transitive naosu; odaiji ni is the stock polite wish.",
